<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 1.24 bln stg more help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 1.24 bln stg more help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 1.24 billion stg of assistance at established interest rates.  </p>
<p>The Bank allotted 276 million outright in bills maturing on or before May 7 and 964 million stg in repos to May 6 and 7.</p>
<p>The Bank has now provided total liquidity of 2.001 billion stg on Tuesday, virtually matching its 2.0 billion money market shortage forecast.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
